/*
 * Fixed Tokyo Night color scheme for rofi.
 *
 * This replaces pywal-generated colors as the target of pywal-theme.rasi.
 * pywal has never actually run on this system (~/.cache/wal doesn't
 * exist), so pywal-theme.rasi was a DANGLING symlink to a file that never
 * existed -- every rofi surface that @imports it (all 8 config-*.rasi
 * variants) has been failing with "Failed to open theme: ... No such file
 * or directory" and rendering completely unstyled this whole time. That
 * was very likely the single biggest source of "rofi looks inconsistent" --
 * it wasn't drifting with pywal, it was silently broken.
 *
 * Also: even had pywal been running, its colors are derived from whatever
 * wallpaper is currently active -- and the wallpaper auto-changer picks a
 * new random one every 30 minutes, which is fundamentally at odds with a
 * stable "Tokyo Night" identity. Fixed colors here instead; see
 * tokyo-day.rasi for the light counterpart DarkLight.sh switches to.
 *
 * REBUILT (2026-09-11): active-background was #9ece6a (green) while
 * selected-normal-background was #7aa2f7 (blue) -- two different accent
 * colors doing the same visual job (border/highlight) depending on which
 * widget you were looking at. Every other themed surface on this system
 * (kitty's url_color, gtk-4.0/tokyo-night-accent.css's accent_bg_color)
 * settled on #7aa2f7 as *the* Tokyo Night accent -- unified to that single
 * color here too. See theme/base.rasi for the structural redesign that
 * consumes these.
 */

* {
    /* Slightly transparent + frosted (blur applied via a Hyprland layer
       rule matched on rofi's layer-shell namespace, see windowrules.lua --
       rofi's own CSS can only set alpha, not blur what's behind it) */
    background:                    rgba(26, 27, 38, 0.90);
    background90:                  rgba(26, 27, 38, 0.90); /* was the typo'd @backrgound90 */
    background-alt:                #24283b;
    foreground:                    #c0caf5;
    foreground-alt:                #565f89;
    selected-normal-background:    #7aa2f7;
    selected-normal-foreground:    #1a1b26;
    active-background:             #7aa2f7;
    active-foreground:             #1a1b26;
    urgent-background:             #f7768e;
    urgent-foreground:             #1a1b26;
}
